---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import ContactCta from '../../components/ContactCta.astro';
---
<Layout title="Entrepreneurship & Perspective — Salim Youssef Najim" description="Salim Youssef Najim’s approach to entrepreneurship: understanding a need, defining a useful idea and working through what it takes to build.">
  <section class="page-hero section-pad"><p class="eyebrow section-index">Ventures / Perspective</p><h1>Business<br/><span>perspective.</span></h1><p class="lead">I’m interested in businesses built around useful products and services. My starting point is the problem, the people it affects and the work needed to solve it.</p></section>
  <section class="focus-section section-pad">
    <div class="section-heading reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow section-index">An engineering approach</p><h2>How I evaluate an idea.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="focus-grid">
      <article class="focus-item reveal"><p class="eyebrow">01 / The need</p><h3>Who is it for?</h3><p>Understand the people, the problem and the alternatives they already have.</p></article>
      <article class="focus-item reveal"><p class="eyebrow">02 / The value</p><h3>What makes it useful?</h3><p>Define what the idea improves and why someone would choose it.</p></article>
      <article class="focus-item reveal"><p class="eyebrow">03 / The work</p><h3>What will it take?</h3><p>Think through the resources, constraints and decisions involved in building it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="venture-principles section-pad">
    <div class="venture-diagram reveal" role="img" aria-label="Approach: understand the need, make something useful, and refine it"><p class="eyebrow">From observation to execution</p><div>Understand <span class="eyebrow">01</span></div><div>Make <span class="eyebrow">02</span></div><div>Refine <span class="eyebrow">03</span></div></div>
    <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow section-index">Across disciplines</p><h2>Engineering is<br/>one way in.</h2><p>Technical thinking helps me examine the details. A business perspective keeps the purpose and the people in view.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">Explore the engineering work <Arrow/></a></div>
  </section>
  <ContactCta/>
</Layout>
